11. Besides the above, this Court is of the considered view that the prayer for quashing - 21 - of FIR and consequential proceedings needs to be accepted for the reason(s): firstly, that the complainant, accused and the victim have deposed .
with one voice that accusation was not intentional and the same stands amicably settled inter se the parties; secondly, the continuance of criminal proceeding(s) will be an exercise in futility when the complainant/victim has decided not to pursue the matter-accusation and buried the hatchet;
Joginder Singh And Another vs State Of Himachal Pradesh & Ors on 12 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/6339282/
12 thirdly, the continuance of the proceedings will give rebirth to enmity and shall certainly disturb the peace and harmony arrived at between the parties; fourthly, the accusation in the instant case falls outside the category of heinous and grave offences as mandated in Para 29.3 in the case of Narinder Singh (supra); fifthly, the continuance of proceedings despite compromise/settlement will certainly be oppressive and prejudicial so as to generate into a weapon of harassment and persecution - 22 - as the petitioners shall have to face the blunt-stigma leading to negativating the settlement/compromise;
sixthly, the continuance of proceedings shall .
unnecessarily burden the docket of the Courts;
seventhly, grant of quietus shall not have any harmful effects on the public and will not in any manner seriously endanger/threaten the well being of the society; eighthly, the continuance of proceedings shall impede the Correctional Objective of Criminal Justice System leading the parties to pre-conviction undergo sufferings and humiliation despite being settled/compromised the matter; ninethly, the State Authorities have neither pointed out any other adversarial circumstances objecting to the settlement/compromise and the prayer for quashing of the proceedings; lastly,
grant of quietus to FIR and consequential proceedings, in terms of the Settlement-Compromise shall secure the ends of justice and enable the parties to lead - 23 - a life of respect and dignity.
